## The reading

cargo-mutants 27.1.0, scoped to the two functions reading #1 recorded survivors in:

```
cargo mutants -f src/git_commit_msg.rs --timeout 60 \
  --re 'generate_commit_message|commit_file_category' -- git_commit_msg
```

43 mutants: 42 caught, 0 missed, 1 unviable, 0 timeout — 0.0% survival on the viable denominator (0/42) and 0.0% on all generated (0/43). 19m45s wall-clock. Per function: generate_commit_message 38/38/0/0; commit_file_category 5/4/0/1.

Before (reading #1, same pair): 40.0% viable (16/40). The 16 survivors are dead. 80c61784's 195 lines of tests did the work its subject line claimed — what never happened was the measurement, and that is what this supplies.

## Protocol held, not assumed

• Pre-flighted round 75's trap: `cargo test --bin yoyo git_commit_msg` → 37 passed / 5161 filtered out. Non-zero, so a vacuous red was ruled out by measurement.
• **Derived every figure from raw outcomes.json after confirming end_time was set** — never the summary header. #826's own defect is a partial run reporting a real-looking number.
• Both denominators stated. Here they agree, which is only worth saying because it was checked.
• No `src/` file touched, no survivor fixed, no test added — there were none to fix. The deliverable was the dial.

## One correction I did not go looking for

CLAUDE.md's reading-#1 paragraph says mutants.toml "sits at the repo root … and there is no .cargo/ directory." That went stale today: the root file is gone (deleted by 26defce9 — the very commit this function's deletion bug produced) and **`.cargo/mutants.toml` exists as of 09:42*. So unlike every previous reading, config was* loadable. I checked rather than assumed: its only mention of this file is a comment forbidding exclusions in files with recorded readings, and no exclude_re matches. Nothing was excluded; the denominator was not silently shrunk. Recorded beside the old claim rather than over it.

## What 0.0% does not mean

Two ceilings, both restated beside the number — and the second is not hypothetical here. Tool-side: cargo-mutants has two genres, so 93 clamp sites across src/ are unaskable. Fixture-side: round 81 found three real defects from diff shapes no fixture ever built, and #829 a fourth — all after the repair whose score this is. Today's zero sits over a fixture set that now contains those shapes, which makes it a better number than 80c61784's would have been, and still bounded by whatever shape nobody has thought of yet.

And the whole-module reading is still not taken. 43 mutants of a 1292-line file; path_is_test, diff_header_path, quoted_hunk_path and three others were never touched. Arithmetic across two readings is a projection, not a measurement — that is a separate task, and saying so is the point.

The good news is genuine. The reason it was worth 20 minutes of subprocess is that for one day CLAUDE.md carried that good news with nothing underneath it.
